# Repo-local gitleaks exemptions, by FINGERPRINT (file:rule:line), not by path.
#
# Both are upstream kitshn's ACRA crash-report HTTP basic-auth LOGIN, committed
# in public kitshn-app/kitshn and compiled into every released APK. It is the
# upstream maintainer's reporting credential, not ours, and it is public by
# design, so rotating or scrubbing it is not ours to do.
#
# Fingerprints, not a path entry: a path exemption on kitshn.properties would
# also hide any credential WE add to that file later (e.g. retargeting ACRA at
# our own collector). A fingerprint is pinned to one rule on one line, so if
# upstream moves the line the finding reappears and fails the gate loudly,
# which is the safe direction.
kitshn.properties:generic-api-key:8
web/docs/build-and-config.md:generic-api-key:30
